{
  "_help": [
    "Each controller has its own table under 'pads': 'dualsense', 'ns_pro' (Switch Pro), 'ns2_pro' (Switch 2 Pro).",
    "A pad's 'buttons' must list every id 0..=32. Change 'type' to one of:",
    "  - 'key'      : set 'value' to a key name from _keyboard_keys below",
    "  - 'macro'    : set 'value' to a macro name defined in 'macros'",
    "  - 'mouse'    : set 'value' to one of: 'left', 'middle', 'right', 'wheel-up', 'wheel-down'",
    "  - 'unbound'  : do nothing (omit 'value')",
    "'trigger_mode': 'l' is ZL / L2 (id 23), 'r' is ZR / R2 (id 24). 'page' = while the trigger is held, the face buttons (ids 0-3) and the D-pad (ids 11-14) use the 'quick_l' (or 'quick_r') page and the trigger itself sends nothing; 'key' = the trigger is an ordinary button with its own binding.",
    "'quick_l' / 'quick_r' may hold only ids 0-3 and 11-14. A missing or unbound id sends nothing while its page is held.",
    "Ids 25..=28 are the four touchpad quadrants (TL/TR/BL/BR).",
    "Switch Pro (Bluetooth): ids by position — B=0 A=1 Y=2 X=3, −=4 Home=5 +=6, LS=7 RS=8, L=9 R=10, D-pad 11-14, ZL=23 ZR=24, Capture=29. Pair it in Windows Bluetooth settings first.",
    "Switch 2 Pro (Bluetooth LE): hold SYNC the first time; afterwards any button reconnects. Do NOT pair it in Windows Bluetooth settings. GL=30 GR=31 C=32; mapping_enabled.ns2_pro=false makes it a virtual Xbox pad (needs ViGEmBus).",
    "Set 'touchpad_cursor_enabled' to false to disable the cursor; sensitivity is in [0.1, 10.0].",
    "'touchpad_midpoint_x' / 'touchpad_midpoint_y' set the quadrant boundary in raw pad coords (default 960/540 = centre of a 1920x1080 pad). If the wrong quadrant fires on click, watch the debug dot in the GUI to see the captured raw position, then tune these values.",
    "mapping_enabled: per-controller switch. true = buttons go through this mapping; false = for DualSense / Switch Pro the app sends nothing and the game reads the controller directly; the Switch 2 Pro instead becomes a virtual Xbox pad (needs ViGEmBus).",
    "rumble_on_connect: true = the controller gives a short buzz when it becomes the active one; false = no buzz.",
    "The window version applies a saved edit automatically while it runs; with --cli, restart the program after editing.",
    "Fields starting with '_' are documentation only and ignored by the program."
  ],
  "_keyboard_keys": {
    "letters_and_digits": [
      "Any single ASCII character is the physical key of the same letter or digit.",
      "Examples: \"x\", \"X\", \"a\", \"0\", \"9\". Case does not matter."
    ],
    "modifiers":   ["Shift", "Control", "Ctrl", "Alt", "Meta", "Win", "Cmd"],
    "modifiers_lr": ["LShift", "RShift", "LControl", "LCtrl", "RControl", "RCtrl", "LAlt", "RAlt"],
    "arrows":      ["Up", "Down", "Left", "Right"],
    "edit_keys":   ["Space", "Enter", "Return", "Tab", "Escape", "Esc", "Backspace", "Delete", "Del"],
    "navigation":  ["Home", "End", "PageUp", "PageDown"],
    "function":    ["F1", "F2", "F3", "F4", "F5", "F6", "F7", "F8", "F9", "F10", "F11", "F12"],
    "punctuation": ["-", "=", "[", "]", "\\", ";", "'", ",", ".", "/", "`"],
    "note": "Unknown key names fail loudly at startup — the validator names the bad binding."
  },

  "version": 2,
  "deadzone": 0.4,
  "trigger_threshold": 0.5,
  "min_press_ms": [8, 25],
  "tick_jitter_ms": [0, 3],
  "log_events": true,
